        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
      <mxCell id="hdr_banner" value="T215 • 6-PANEL CONCEPT DOSSIER • ENTERPRISE CONTROL &amp; DATA PLANE LENS • REGULATED ENTERPRISE
Data Model vs. Ontology: 6-Panel Executive Dossier &amp; Ladder of Meaning
Why Data Models Dictate How Records Are Stored (Closed-World) While Ontologies Enable Machine Reasoning (Open-World)
Stack Anchor: Google Cloud Vertex AI + Spanner Graph + Model Armor + OpenTelemetry  |  KPIs: 99.95% Control Plane SLO · Zero-Trust OBO · Unified Ontology Graph" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=8;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#4F46E5;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#0F172A;fontFamily=Inter,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingRight=12;spacingTop=10;spacingBottom=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
        <mxGeometry x="28" y="24" width="864" height="116" as="geometry" />
      </mxCell>
      <mxCell id="SubBanner" value="GOVERNANCE &amp; PERSONA CONTRACT: ARB Invariant: Decouple reasoning state and semantic ontology from single-app schemas.
HIPAA / SOX / GxP Deterministic Audit Trail • VPC-SC + Customer-Managed Encryption (CMEK)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=8;fillColor=#DBEAFE;strokeColor=#4F46E5;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#0F172A;fontFamily=Inter,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingRight=12;spacingTop=10;spacingBottom=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
        <mxGeometry x="28" y="150" width="864" height="42" as="geometry" />
      </mxCell>
      <mxCell id="dossier_p_1" value="01 • THE CORE ANALOGY
Library Card Catalog vs. Collective Wisdom
Data Model = Card Catalog (tells you where every book is stored, zero understanding of contents).
Ontology = Collective Intelligence (connects ideas across books to infer new knowledge)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=8;fillColor=#ECFDF5;strokeColor=#059669;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#0F172A;fontFamily=Inter,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingRight=12;spacingTop=10;spacingBottom=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
        <mxGeometry x="28" y="208" width="268" height="400" as="geometry" />
      </mxCell>
      <mxCell id="dossier_p_2" value="02 • HEAD-TO-HEAD &amp; WORLD ASSUMPTION
Closed-World vs. Open-World Logic
• Scope: Single App Schema vs Shared Enterprise Domain
• Closed-World (Data Model): Missing fact = FALSE
• Open-World (Ontology): Missing fact = UNKNOWN (open for discovery)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=8;fillColor=#EFF6FF;strokeColor=#2563EB;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#0F172A;fontFamily=Inter,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingRight=12;spacingTop=10;spacingBottom=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
        <mxGeometry x="326" y="208" width="268" height="400" as="geometry" />
      </mxCell>
      <mxCell id="dossier_p_3" value="03 • KEY CAPABILITIES CONTRAST
Storage Efficiency vs. Machine Reasoning
Data Model Can: Enforce table structure, run fast OLTP queries, power standard reports.
Ontology Can: Represent semantic meaning, infer hidden relationships, unify silos for AI." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=8;fillColor=#F5F3FF;strokeColor=#7C3AED;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#0F172A;fontFamily=Inter,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingRight=12;spacingTop=10;spacingBottom=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
        <mxGeometry x="624" y="208" width="268" height="400" as="geometry" />
      </mxCell>
      <mxCell id="dossier_p_4" value="04 • THE 5-RUNG LADDER OF MEANING
From Free-Text Tags to Formal Logic
Rung 1: Folksonomy (Free-text tags)
Rung 2: Controlled Vocabulary (Standard terms)
Rung 3: Taxonomy (Parent-child hierarchy)
Rung 4: Thesaurus (Associative synonyms)
Rung 5: Ontology (Formal axioms &amp; AI reasoning)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=8;fillColor=#ECFDF5;strokeColor=#059669;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#0F172A;fontFamily=Inter,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingRight=12;spacingTop=10;spacingBottom=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
        <mxGeometry x="28" y="636" width="268" height="400" as="geometry" />
      </mxCell>
      <mxCell id="dossier_p_5" value="05 • 6-STEP ONTOLOGY REASONING FLOW
How AI Turns Facts into Decisions
1. Ingest multi-source data -&gt; 2. Map to ontology concepts -&gt; 3. Apply OWL/SHACL rules -&gt; 4. Infer new links -&gt; 5. Answer multi-hop queries -&gt; 6. Learn &amp; evolve continuously." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=8;fillColor=#EFF6FF;strokeColor=#2563EB;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#0F172A;fontFamily=Inter,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingRight=12;spacingTop=10;spacingBottom=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
        <mxGeometry x="326" y="636" width="268" height="400" as="geometry" />
      </mxCell>
      <mxCell id="dossier_p_6" value="06 • BETTER TOGETHER EQUATION
Data Model (The How) + Ontology (The What)
Data models organize storage; Ontologies give it machine-verifiable meaning.
Combined Power: Breaks data silos · Unified enterprise meaning · Smarter agent decisions." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=8;fillColor=#F5F3FF;strokeColor=#7C3AED;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#0F172A;fontFamily=Inter,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingRight=12;spacingTop=10;spacingBottom=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
        <mxGeometry x="624" y="636" width="268" height="400" as="geometry" />
      </mxCell>
